    <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>

    <details class="faq" open>
      <summary>Is online poker legal in the Philippines?</summary>
      <p>
        For Philippine residents, the legal situation is nuanced. PAGCOR licenses certain domestic online gaming
        operators (PIGOs), but most international rooms in this review are not PAGCOR-licensed and operate under
        offshore licenses. Players use these rooms commonly without enforcement against individual users, but
        the activity is not formally regulated as legal in PH. We recommend players consult their own legal
        counsel and understand their tax obligations on winnings.
      </p>
    </details>

    <details class="faq">
      <summary>What's the best deposit method for Filipino players?</summary>
      <p>
        Bitcoin (BTC) is the most universally accepted, fastest, and lowest-friction option across the rooms
        in this review. E-wallets like Skrill and Neteller work on most rooms. Card deposits are workable on
        WPT Global and a few others but unreliable elsewhere. GCash direct integration with international rooms
        is rare; most players who use GCash route through a BTC exchange like PDAX or Coins.ph.
      </p>
    </details>

    <details class="faq">
      <summary>Do I need a VPN to play?</summary>
      <p>
        For ClubGG, Natural8, WPT Global, and CoinPoker — no, in most cases. These rooms accept PH players
        directly. ACR sometimes triggers geo-checks that resolve with support but may benefit from a VPN if
        you experience friction. PokerStars often requires a VPN due to geo-restrictions. Note that using a
        VPN may violate the terms of service on some rooms and can lead to account closure if detected, so
        verify each room's policy before using one.
      </p>
    </details>

    <details class="faq">
      <summary>Are these sites safe for my money?</summary>
      <p>
        The five rooms ranked #1–#5 are all established operators with multi-year track records of player
        fund safety. None has had a major incident with player balances in the past 5+ years. As with any
        online platform, we recommend not keeping more on the site than you need for active play, and using
        BTC withdrawals for fast retrieval of significant balances.
      </p>
    </details>

    <details class="faq">
      <summary>Can I play with PHP (Philippine Pesos)?</summary>
      <p>
        Most international rooms denominate in USD and convert at deposit and withdrawal. Direct PHP support
        is rare on the rooms in this review. The practical workflow for PH players is: PHP → BTC (via PDAX
        or Coins.ph) → poker site, with the reverse on withdrawal. Conversion fees are typically 1–2% per leg.
      </p>
    </details>

    <details class="faq">
      <summary>Can I deposit with GCash?</summary>
      <p>
        Direct GCash → poker site integration is uncommon. The standard workaround is GCash → PDAX or Coins.ph
        → BTC → poker site, which takes about 10–15 minutes total and incurs minimal fees. Some payment
        intermediaries claim GCash-to-poker rails but most are unreliable; the BTC route remains the cleanest.
      </p>
    </details>

    <details class="faq">
      <summary>How much should I deposit to start?</summary>
      <p>
        The traditional bankroll guideline is 20–40 buy-ins for the stake you intend to play. For someone
        starting at $0.05/$0.10 NL ($10 buy-in), that's a $200–400 starting bankroll. For $0.50/$1 NL ($100 buy-in),
        $2,000–$4,000. Tournaments require larger rolls due to higher variance — typically 100+ buy-ins for
        the level you play. Don't deposit more than you can comfortably lose.
      </p>
    </details>

    <details class="faq">
      <summary>What about the welcome bonuses — are they actually worth it?</summary>
      <p>
        Most welcome bonuses unlock incrementally as you generate rake. A "100% up to $1,000" bonus typically
        means you earn $1 of bonus released for every $5–10 in rake you generate, capped at $1,000 over a
        time window (often 60–90 days). If you play seriously, you'll unlock most or all of it. If you play
        casually, you'll release a small fraction. Don't deposit larger than you'd play just to chase a
        bonus you can't realistically clear.
      </p>
    </details>
  </section>

